---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { personSchema } from "../lib/schema";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";

const schema = [personSchema()];
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Operator shipping in public across sectors." schema={schema} ogImage="/og-about.png">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1 class="sr-only">About Jordan Newell</h1>
    <p>
      Jordan Newell. Software takes the front seat — a growing collection of projects
      shipping into the world, built on a self-hosted fleet of AI agents running
      around the clock and the infrastructure behind mail, status pages, and sites
      for real businesses. Also on the plate: DW Trim as Managing Partner.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>DW Trim.</strong> Dante Woodson's carpentry company — central and
      south Florida, proven craft, real customer base. I came in as Managing
      Partner to run everything that isn't the craft: ops, tech, the scaling
      side. We're explicit about the split — Dante is senior in the trade and
      trains me on it; I'm senior in growth and build the systems that let the
      trade scale. Before this I ran NewellsWork, B2B contractor services —
      bidding, estimation, project management. Half-dead now, but the playbook
      and the scars carried straight over. The bet: prove the playbook on a
      business that already works, then use it again on the next one.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>The operator's desk.</strong> Field notes, post-mortems,
      manifestos when warranted.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
